      ],
      "text": "Role in hyponatremia:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " severe, rapid-onset or highly Sx: partial rapid correction w hypertonic (3%) saline; sz or other severe neuro Sx: rapid ↑Na by 4 to 6 mEq/L, monitored in ICU w Na Q2 h"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Rate limits:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " too-rapid correction can cause osmotic demyelination syndrome; ≤ 8 mEq/L ↑ over first 24 h; ⍉faster than 0.5 mEq/L/h, except first few hrs of severe hyponatremia (up to 2 mEq/L/h)"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
